{
  "case_id": "2010-09-152",
  "document_hash": "ac3219cbe96a3b94c6bf50dc633a2dcea9ee6818755033ad8ec345a4ba5dca09",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Supreme Court",
      "case_id": "2010-09-152",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ac3219cbe96a3b94c6bf50dc633a2dcea9ee6818755033ad8ec345a4ba5dca09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ac3219cbe96a-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 1:00 p.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2010-09-152",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ac3219cbe96a3b94c6bf50dc633a2dcea9ee6818755033ad8ec345a4ba5dca09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ac3219cbe96a-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FREDERICK: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: This case involves a vaccine designed in the 1940s that was administered to Hannah Bruesewitz in 1992, some 30 years after scientists discovered a safer way to design the pertussis component of the DTP vaccine."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2010-09-152",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ac3219cbe96a3b94c6bf50dc633a2dcea9ee6818755033ad8ec345a4ba5dca09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ac3219cbe96a-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: What is -- I'm sorry, Mr. Frederick. What's the point that you are trying to make?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2010-09-152",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ac3219cbe96a3b94c6bf50dc633a2dcea9ee6818755033ad8ec345a4ba5dca09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ac3219cbe96a-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: But you haven't really answered Justice Alito's question as to why the later language is not surplus."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2010-09-152",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ac3219cbe96a3b94c6bf50dc633a2dcea9ee6818755033ad8ec345a4ba5dca09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ac3219cbe96a-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Mr. Frederick, I have this problem with -- with your interpretation. As -- as has been said, the government interprets \"unavoidable\" to mean unavoidable with respect to the vaccine that has been approved."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2010-09-152",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "ac3219cbe96a3b94c6bf50dc633a2dcea9ee6818755033ad8ec345a4ba5dca09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ac3219cbe96a-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Anyone could go to the State -- I mean, somebody who won in the vaccine court could go to court on the argument that the amount was insufficient, the amount of compensation. There is -- there is no foreclosure of anyone to come to court; is that right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2010-09-152",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "ac3219cbe96a3b94c6bf50dc633a2dcea9ee6818755033ad8ec345a4ba5dca09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ac3219cbe96a-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Does the secretary -- does the secretary have the authority to -- to withdraw certification on the ground that it is no longer safe, fair, and potent?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2010-09-152",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "ac3219cbe96a3b94c6bf50dc633a2dcea9ee6818755033ad8ec345a4ba5dca09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ac3219cbe96a-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. SULLIVAN: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: Congress enacted the National Childhood Vaccine Injury Act against the backdrop of a wave of tort litigation that threatened to drive manufacturers out of the business of providing the vaccine -\u00ad"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2010-09-152",
      "confidence": 0.88,
      "document_hash": "ac3219cbe96a3b94c6bf50dc633a2dcea9ee6818755033ad8ec345a4ba5dca09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ac3219cbe96a-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Ms. Sullivan -- Ms. Sullivan, if Congress had wanted to do that, they could have said simply that no vaccine manufacturer may be held civilly liable if the vaccine is properly prepared and accompanied by proper directions and adequate warnings."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2010-09-152",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ac3219cbe96a3b94c6bf50dc633a2dcea9ee6818755033ad8ec345a4ba5dca09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ac3219cbe96a-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: If Congress were so clear, as you are describing it, then why didn't it adopt the provision that said failure to develop a safer vaccine would not be grounds for liability?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source",
      "case_id": "2010-09-152",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ac3219cbe96a3b94c6bf50dc633a2dcea9ee6818755033ad8ec345a4ba5dca09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ac3219cbe96a-0002-0009",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Congress was worried about episodic waves of fear about vaccines leading to future litigation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2010-09-152",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ac3219cbe96a3b94c6bf50dc633a2dcea9ee6818755033ad8ec345a4ba5dca09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ac3219cbe96a-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: You are making an assumption that has a flawed premise, which is that their only concern was protecting the manufacturers."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Sullivan",
      "case_id": "2010-09-152",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ac3219cbe96a3b94c6bf50dc633a2dcea9ee6818755033ad8ec345a4ba5dca09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ac3219cbe96a-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Two purposes: Compensation and the protection of the vaccine supply."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2010-09-152",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ac3219cbe96a3b94c6bf50dc633a2dcea9ee6818755033ad8ec345a4ba5dca09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ac3219cbe96a-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: I'm still not clear -- I'm still not clear what answer you gave to Justice Ginsburg's question, saying: Why didn't Congress put this out in plain words: There should be no liability for design? Is the answer sloppy drafting?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2010-09-152",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ac3219cbe96a3b94c6bf50dc633a2dcea9ee6818755033ad8ec345a4ba5dca09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ac3219cbe96a-0002-0005",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think the Court finds itself actually three-quarters of the way through the argument without actually hearing about the most important federal agency that is involved with this, which is arguably not the Food and Drug Administration but the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2010-09-152",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ac3219cbe96a3b94c6bf50dc633a2dcea9ee6818755033ad8ec345a4ba5dca09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ac3219cbe96a-0002-0006",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CDC has to recommend it for routine administration. And that is a judgment that CDC makes with the advice of the Advisory Committee on Immunization Practices."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. FREDERICK",
      "case_id": "2010-09-152",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ac3219cbe96a3b94c6bf50dc633a2dcea9ee6818755033ad8ec345a4ba5dca09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ac3219cbe96a-0003-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In 1965 Lederle's researchers determine that Lily, the Tri-Solgen, had a \"superior product,\" that's at page 245 of the Joint Appendix."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Alderson Reporting Company",
      "case_id": "2010-09-152",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ac3219cbe96a3b94c6bf50dc633a2dcea9ee6818755033ad8ec345a4ba5dca09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ac3219cbe96a-0003-0000",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "They had made the determination they were not capable internally of doing a safer design and they knew that for eight years and they nonetheless kept the wholesale pertussis in its market and the documents in this case indicate they did it for economic reasons."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2010-09-152",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ac3219cbe96a3b94c6bf50dc633a2dcea9ee6818755033ad8ec345a4ba5dca09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ac3219cbe96a-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Their argument is that the CDC will do it better than juries. That's what I heard him say."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2010-09-152",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ac3219cbe96a3b94c6bf50dc633a2dcea9ee6818755033ad8ec345a4ba5dca09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ac3219cbe96a-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: I'm just trying to find out what your position is on that. Do they compare it to existing vaccines or not?"
    },
    {
